<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Josiah Zion Gumede</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a>–<a href="/years/1989">1989</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josiah">Josiah</a> Zion Gumede was a Zimbabwean politician of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abel-muzorewa">Abel Muzorewa</a>'s United African National Council. Under the internal settlement he became the first and only president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a> Rhodesia from June to December 1979, a largely ceremonial post. The arrangement ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lancaster-house">Lancaster House</a> Agreement and the country's independence as Zimbabwe in 1980.</p></div>
